          >
            ₹10,00,000
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p
        class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-700"
      >
        A two-day Maharashtrian wedding for 200 guests in Mumbai on a ₹10,00,000 budget: Day 1 brings Halad Chadavne (haldi), mehendi and a family Sangeet, and Day 2 is the Simant Pujan, Antarpat, Mangalashtak and Saptapadi followed by a short evening reception. Catering and the venue take over half the budget, so we assumed a banquet hall in Dadar, Thane or Navi Mumbai rather than a hotel ballroom, a pure-vegetarian traditional menu, and that most guests live in or near Mumbai. With about four months to go, venue, caterer and photographer should be locked in this month because good Muhurat dates book out fast.
      </p>
    </header>
    <section
      class="mb-10 break-inside-avoid"
    >
      <h2
        class="text-xl font-bold border-b border-neutral-300 pb-2 mb-4 text-neutral-900"
      >
        1. Budget Allocation
      </h2>
      <div
        class="overflow-x-auto"
      >
        <table
          class="w-full text-left text-sm border border-neutral-200"
        >
          <caption
            class="sr-only"
          >
            Budget allocation by category
          </caption>
          <thead
            class="bg-neutral-100 text-neutral-700 uppercase text-xs"
          >
            <tr>
              <th
                class="p-2.5 border-b border-r border-neutral-200"
                scope="col"
              >
                Category
              </th>
              <th
                class="p-2.5 border-b border-r border-neutral-200 text-right"
                scope="col"
              >
                Cost
              </th>
              <th
                class="p-2.5 border-b border-r border-neutral-200 text-right"
                scope="col"
              >
                %
              </th>
              <th
                class="p-2.5 border-b border-neutral-200"
                scope="col"
              >
                Guidance & Tips
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody
            class="divide-y divide-neutral-200"
          >
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Venue & Decor
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹2,20,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                22
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Book a banquet hall for two days on a weekday-evening or package rate and ask for the basic stage and lighting to be included. Reuse the Day 2 mandap flowers for the reception backdrop.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Catering
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹3,00,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                30
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Choose a traditional Maharashtrian thali (puran poli, masale bhaat, varan-bhaat, shrikhand) at ₹900 to ₹1,100 per plate instead of a multi-cuisine buffet, and confirm a final headcount two weeks out to avoid paying for extra plates.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Photography & Videography
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹80,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                8
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Hire one lead photographer plus one candid shooter for Day 2 and a single photographer for the Day 1 functions. Skip the drone and the printed album, and take a digital gallery instead.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Attire, Jewellery & Beauty
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹1,30,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                13
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Buy the bride's Paithani or Nauvari saree and rent the groom's pheta and sherwani set. Rent statement jewellery such as the nath and tanmani for the ceremony and use family heirlooms for the rest.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Priest, Rituals & Music
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹50,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                5
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Ask the priest for one consolidated samagri list and buy it in bulk from a Dadar market wholesaler. Book a single sanai and dhol-tasha group for both the varat and the ceremony.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Mehendi, Sangeet & Haldi
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹60,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                6
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Keep the Sangeet a family-performance evening with a DJ for two hours rather than a hired choreographer, and use fresh marigold and turmeric from the market for the haldi set-up.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Guest Accommodation & Transport
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹60,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                6
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Block rooms only for out-of-town elders at a budget hotel near the venue, and arrange a single hired tempo traveller for the varat and airport or station pick-ups.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Invitations & Gifts
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹30,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                3
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Send a WhatsApp e-invite to most guests and print cards only for elders and close relatives. Choose a useful return gift such as a potted tulsi or a steel dabba.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr
              class="odd:bg-white even:bg-neutral-50/50"
            >
              <td
                class="p-2.5 font-medium border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                Contingency
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                ₹70,000
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-right font-mono border-r border-neutral-200"
              >
                7
                %
              </td>
              <td
                class="p-2.5 text-neutral-600 text-xs"
              >
                Hold this reserve back until the final week. It typically absorbs last-minute headcount increases, extra decor flowers and vendor overtime.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <tfoot
            class="bg-neutral-100 font-semibold border-t-2 border-neutral-300"
