            class="font-semibold text-sm text-neutral-900 mb-1"
          >
            Paithani-inspired mandap
          </h3>
          <p
            class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed"
          >
            Drape the stage in peacock and lotus Paithani motifs in maroon, gold and green, with marigold and mogra garlands. It photographs beautifully and reads as unmistakably Maharashtrian.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded border border-neutral-200 p-3.5 bg-white break-inside-avoid"
        >
          <h3
            class="font-semibold text-sm text-neutral-900 mb-1"
          >
            Dhol-tasha varat entrance
          </h3>
          <p
            class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed"
          >
            Welcome the groom's procession with a dhol-tasha troupe and a sanai player, then switch to soft sanai for the Antarpat moment so the energy builds toward the ceremony.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded border border-neutral-200 p-3.5 bg-white break-inside-avoid"
        >
          <h3
            class="font-semibold text-sm text-neutral-900 mb-1"
          >
            Eco-friendly haldi
          </h3>
          <p
            class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed"
          >
            Use fresh turmeric paste, marigold petals and a mango-leaf toran instead of synthetic colour, and let guests apply it with small brass bowls that double as return gifts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded border border-neutral-200 p-3.5 bg-white break-inside-avoid"
        >
          <h3
            class="font-semibold text-sm text-neutral-900 mb-1"
          >
            Tulsi sapling return gifts
          </h3>
          <p
            class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed"
          >
            Gift each family a small tulsi sapling in a clay pot with a handwritten thank-you tag. It is affordable, sustainable and ties back to the Griha Pravesh tradition.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded border border-neutral-200 p-3.5 bg-white break-inside-avoid"
        >
          <h3
            class="font-semibold text-sm text-neutral-900 mb-1"
          >
            Street-food reception counter
          </h3>
          <p
            class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed"
          >
            Add a small live counter of vada pav, misal and cutting chai at the evening reception, a nostalgic Mumbai touch that is cheaper than an extra buffet station.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="rounded border border-neutral-200 p-3.5 bg-white break-inside-avoid"
        >
          <h3
            class="font-semibold text-sm text-neutral-900 mb-1"
          >
            Sangeet family story reel
          </h3>
          <p
            class="text-xs text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed"
          >
